  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-24 (independent auditor, authored none of 9c3697d0d1). RFC 7606 Section 5.2: \"For this reason, if any path attribute errors are encountered in such an UPDATE message and if any encountered error specifies an error-handling approach other than \"attribute discard\", then the \"session reset\" approach MUST be used.\" The only change to TestRFC7606EmptyMPReachEscalatesToReset is the call, now ValidateUpdateRFC7606Peer(attrs, legacyNLRI, false, false, nil, false, false): acceptASSet=false is RFC 9774's default and the unit's AS_PATH carries no set segment, so no input or verdict path moved. Its cases still assert exact outcomes on the population boundary: empty MP_REACH plus ORIGIN=3 gives SessionReset with AttrCode 1; the same error beside reachable MP NLRI or legacy NLRI gives TreatAsWithdraw; an attribute-discard-only error stays AttributeDiscard (code 7, one entry); an abandoned walk escalates only without reachable NLRI. Producer read at HEAD: the post-walk escalation (!hasReachableNLRI && hasAttrOtherThanMPUnreach && strongest > AttributeDiscard) is unchanged. Other carriers unchanged; rfc9830_nlri_receive_test.go working copy equals HEAD. Unit ran green at HEAD.",
